  "raw_text": "88\n\nWatla ba main kaikaia warkka\n \n–\n \nbuilding maintenance work\n \n/ trabajo de mantenimiento de\nedificios\n\nMain kaikras kaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto neglect, to not care for, to not protect\n \n/ descuidar, no cuidar, no proteger\n\nMain kakaira\n \n(n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \nwatcher, guard\n \n/ vigilante, guardia\n\n(Construct:\n \nMain kakairika\n)\n\nSîp main kakaira\n \n(n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \nshepherd\n \n/ pastor\n \n(Alt:\n \nSepad\n)\n\nMain mai kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto mind you, to take care of you, to watch you, to guard you\n \n/ cuidarte, protegerte\n\nMan kaikankam ra...\n \n–\n \nFrom your point of view\n…\n \n/ Desde tu punto de vista\n…\n\nMisbara kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto hate, to detest\n \n/ odiar, detestar\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu-07/19\n):\n \nTasba uplika nani ba dîa muni misbara wan kaikisa ki?\n \n–\n \nWhy do people of the world hate us?\n \n/ ¿Por\nqué la gente del mundo nos odia?)\n\nPainkira kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto view as fine/pretty/good/beautiful/lovely; to see well\n \n/ ver como\nbien/bonita/buena/hermosa/ encantadora; ver bien\n\nParam kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto see clearly\n \n/ ver claramente\n\nPi kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto taste\n \n/ probar\n\nPitka kat kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto look at things in an appropriate way, to be optimistic\n \n/ mirar las cosas de manera\napropiada, ser optimista\n\nPraki kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto compare\n \n/ comparar\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nfy18\n):\n \nwal praki kaikisa\n \n–\n \ncompares with\n \n/ se compara con\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\ndb\n-\nAiseya\n \n40:25\n):\n \npraki ai kaikaisma\n \n–\n \nyou compare me\n \n/\n \nme comparas\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu\n-\n07/21\n):\n \nD\nî\na muni Jehova upla wala nani wal praki wan kaikras?\n \n–\n \nWhy does Jehovah not compare us with\n\nothers?\n \n/ ¿Por qué no nos compara Jehová con\n \nlos demás?\n)\n\nPraki kaikanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ncomparison, illustration\n \n/ comparación, ilustración\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nth-8\n):\n \nPraki kaikanka nani wal smalkaia\n \n–\n \nTo teach with illustrations\n \n/ Enseñar con ilustraciones)\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nPraki kaikanka kum aisas\n \n–\n \nGive an illustration\n \n/ Dar una ilustración)\n\nPraki kaikanka isi\n \n–\n \nsimple illustration\n \n/ ilustración sencilla\n\nSilp luki kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto examine by oneself, to meditate\n \n/ examinarse a sí mismo, meditar\n\nTanis kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto view as foolishness\n \n/ ver como una tontería\n\nTihu luki kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto deeply examine, to consider deeply, to analyze deeply, to meditate\n \n/ examinar\nprofundamente, considerar profundamente, analizar profundamente, meditar\n\nTihu luki kaikanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ndeep thought, deep thinking, meditation\n \n/ pensamiento profundo, meditación\n\nTnatka raya ra kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto see in a new way\n \n/ ver de una nueva manera\n\nTrai kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto try, to attempt\n \n/ intentar\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \ntrai kaiki kan\n \n–\n \nwas trying\n \n/ estaba intentando)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb60\n):\n \nKunin ai munaia trai kaikisma\n \n–\n \nYou are trying to trick me\n \n/ Intentas engañarme)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu\n-\n10/19\n):\n \nDîa muni yawan\n \ntrai kaikaia sa ki lalah ra latwan kaikaia apia?\n \n–\n \nWhy must we try not to love money?\n \n/\n\n¿Por qué debemos tratar de no amar el dinero?\n)\n\nTraika kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto tempt, to test\n \n/ tentar\n\n(Note/Nota: It does not mean\n \nto suffer\n \n/ No significa\n \n“\nsufrir\n”\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-Jems 1:13\n):\n \nupla ra sin witin mita traika kaikras\n \n–\n \nhe does not tempt anyone\n \n/ el no prueba a nadie)\n\nTraika kaikanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ntrial, test, temptation\n \n/ juicio, prueba, tentación\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-10/20\n):\n \nTraika kaikanka mapara sna taim, dîa daukisna?\n \n–\n \nWhen I am facing a temptation,\nwhat do I do?\n \n/ Cuando me enfrento a una tentación, qué hago?)\n\nUmpira kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto have mercy, to extend mercy\n, to have compassion\n \n/ tener piedad, extender misericordia,\ntener compasión\n\nUmpira kaikras\n \n–\n \nnot having mercy, not extending mercy\n \n/ no tener piedad, no extender misericordia\n\nUmpira kaikan lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nmerciful way,\n \nmercy, compassion\n \n/ de forma misericordiosa, misericordia,\n\ncompasión\n\nUmpira kaikan lâka marikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto show mercy, to show compassion\n \n/ mostrar misericordia, mostrar\ncompasión\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu-06/19\n):\n \nUmpira kaikan lâka markisa kaka, yawan dîa daukbia apia bara dîa muni?\n \n–\n \nIf we show mercy,\nwhat will we not do and why?\n \n/ Si mostramos misericordia, ¿qué no haremos y por qué?)\n\nWih kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto go to see, to go to visit\n \n/ ir a ver, ir a visitar",
